{"term":"absent","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7914bf1a9ce3366f03","definition":"Being away from a place; withdrawn from a place; existing but not present; (sometimes) missing.","example":"Owing to his own illness and then his family's, Ramzi has often been absent from class this month. We will help him catch up with his studies.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["present"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["absentation","absentative","absently","absentment","absentness","absent over leave","absent referent","absent treatment","absent voter","absent without leave","nonabsent","omniabsent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0d7e21433c1581c7ea","definition":"Not existing.","example":"The body part was rudimentary or absent in 1% of specimens.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["present","existing","extant"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["absentation","absentative","absently","absentment","absentness","absent over leave","absent referent","absent treatment","absent voter","absent without leave","nonabsent","omniabsent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1dafdc7656bc9b58cd","definition":"Inattentive to what is passing; absent-minded; preoccupied.","example":"Tom was there, but he seemed absent and withdrawn. Normally he is quite present [= engaged] during a meeting.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["present"],"collocations":[],"usage":"comparable","register":"comparable","wordFamily":["absentation","absentative","absently","absentment","absentness","absent over leave","absent referent","absent treatment","absent voter","absent without leave","no